  "statement": "Compute the largest possible radius of a circle contained in the region defined by \\(|x + |y||\\leq 1\\) in the coordinate plane.",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "\\boxed {2\\sqrt{2} - 2 = 2(\\sqrt{2} - 1)}",
    "value": "\\boxed {2\\sqrt{2} - 2 = 2(\\sqrt{2} - 1)}"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2025-p5.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "After drawing the graph, it's clear that the circle should pass through \\((- 1,0)\\) and be tangent to \\(y = x - 1\\) and \\(y = - x + 1\\) . Letting the radius of this circle be \\(r\\) , we have \\(r\\sqrt{2} +r = 2\\) , so \\(\\boxed {r = 2\\sqrt{2} - 2}\\) .\n\n[One or more solution diagrams were omitted from this imported transcription.]",
